# Trellis Studio settings. Copy to packages/studio/.env and fill in what you need.
# `make up` / `./trellis-up` writes TRELLIS_JWT_SECRET (and TRELLIS_PORTAL_SECRET, when it can copy it) here for you,
# the same value as Resource Explorer's and Egeria Advisor's .env.
# Studio is started by packages/studio/scripts/start-studio.sh (`make studio-web` / `make up-studio`), which loads this
# file without overriding values already set in the environment.

# ── Required ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Signs Studio's session tokens. It must be the SAME value in every Trellis app's .env (RE, EA, Studio): one sign-in
# then works across them. There is no Studio-only override and no derived default; Studio refuses sign-ins without it.
# trellis-up generates it once if no app has one: `openssl rand -hex 32` makes one by hand.
TRELLIS_JWT_SECRET=

# ── Egeria ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Egeria platform and view server (EGERIA_VIEW_SERVER_URL, EA's name, is accepted too).
EGERIA_PLATFORM_URL=https://localhost:9443
EGERIA_VIEW_SERVER=qs-view-server
# Studio has NO service account: every Egeria call runs as the signed-in user. Never set EGERIA_USER /
# EGERIA_USER_PASSWORD here (they are pyegeria's CLI-only names); the start script unsets them.

# ── Sign-in ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Egeria user ids no person may sign in to Studio as (comma-separated): list EA's own service account here.
# RE's service account (RE_DAEMON_USER_ID) is refused too when it is set.
TRELLIS_SERVICE_ACCOUNTS=
# RE_DAEMON_USER_ID=
# How long a Studio session lasts, in hours (default 8; Egeria's own token caps it at about 1 hour).
# STUDIO_JWT_TTL_HOURS=8
# The login policy is trellis-auth's shared one: TRELLIS_REQUIRE_LOGIN (default true), TRELLIS_ANONYMOUS_READ
# (development only), TRELLIS_PUBLIC_PATHS; each can be set per app as STUDIO_<NAME>.

# ── Portal single sign-on (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# The Portal's SSO secret: the same value as the Portal's EGERIA_ADVISOR_SSO_SECRET. Empty: Portal SSO is off.
# STUDIO_PORTAL_SECRET overrides it for Studio only.
TRELLIS_PORTAL_SECRET=
# Origins allowed to hand a Portal token to Studio by postMessage (comma-separated), e.g. http://localhost:8885
STUDIO_PORTAL_ORIGINS=

# ── Where things are ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Studio's own public origin. Egeria Advisor's ADVISOR_EMBED_ORIGINS must list it, so EA can be embedded here.
STUDIO_PUBLIC_URL=http://localhost:8840
# Where the embedded Egeria Advisor panel loads from.
EGERIA_ADVISOR_URL=http://localhost:8880/
